    "change_policy": "A published (active or retired) version never changes: its digest is pinned in published_digests and recomputed by npm run verify. A new model, effort, multiplier, cap or price is a new version. A version is published only with the owner's recorded confirmation (ADR-0022, Pending owner confirmation). Each run shape (per_product without run_shape, for listings-run@1; agent_loop, for agent-run@1) has its own active pointer in active_versions, so a loop version publishes while a per-product version stays active (ADR-0027 item 4). ADR-0036 removed the unrecovered-cost cap: version 1 keeps its published workspace_period_unrecovered_cost_cap_usd, which nothing enforces, and no later version carries one. ADR-0039 made credits the only spend limit: versions 1 and 3 keep their published run_cost_cap_usd and workspace_daily_cost_cap_usd, which nothing enforces once version 4 is active; version 4 and every later per-product version, and every loop version, carry neither (nor a look-for-work cap). The owner chose the best model for every agent (2026-10-26): from version 4, every version of either run shape holds only Claude Opus 5.5 entries (npm run verify refuses any other model, an older or newer Opus included; a later model needs a reviewed change to that rule); Haiku 5.5 and Sonnet 5.5 stay only in the versions published or proposed before it.",
